604
00:35:09,421 --> 00:35:16,420
flavors.

605
00:35:16,421 --> 00:35:19,420
But if you're looking for a candy that delivers a party in your

606
00:35:19,421 --> 00:35:23,420
mouth worthy of a carnival or theme park, this fluffy favorite

607
00:35:23,421 --> 00:35:27,420
from the 19th century is the only way to go.

608
00:35:27,421 --> 00:35:33,420
And you won't believe how little sugar it takes to create it.

609
00:35:33,421 --> 00:35:37,420
During World War II, Hershey produced a chocolate bar called

610
00:35:37,421 --> 00:35:42,020
called Field Ration D that was melt-resistant, high in protein,

611
00:35:42,021 --> 00:35:45,560
and most importantly, not very tasty.

612
00:35:45,561 --> 00:35:48,760
It wasn't intended for pleasure, but to stave off starvation.

613
00:35:51,860 --> 00:35:55,580
The Italians call it zuccherofilato, meaning sugar

614
00:35:55,581 --> 00:35:56,780
thread.

615
00:35:56,781 --> 00:36:01,080
The French, la barba papa, or papa's beard.

616
00:36:01,081 --> 00:36:06,220
The Dutch, sucerspin, literally sugar spider.

617
00:36:06,221 --> 00:36:09,760
By any name, cotton candy is unique.

618
00:36:09,761 --> 00:36:13,860
No other sweet treat looks like a giant pastel cotton ball.

619
00:36:13,861 --> 00:36:17,260
It reminds us of a simpler era when our parents and their

620
00:36:17,261 --> 00:36:21,260
parents enjoyed the very same taste at bygone carnivals

621
00:36:21,261 --> 00:36:25,080
and county fairs. Part of the fun of cotton candy

622
00:36:25,081 --> 00:36:28,580
